    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i dont know if i can do the minute at a time thing. it feels like i'm just waiting for something that's never coming back. it's not just being lonely... it feels like there's no point in being here if the only person i want to talk to isn't. it's like my whole purpose was tied to him and now i'm just a ghost in this house.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you feel like a ghost—when your whole world was built around someone, their absence can make you feel invisible to yourself. But you're not just a leftover echo; you're a person who loved deeply, and that love doesn't disappear even if it has nowhere to go. The point isn't to find a new purpose overnight—it's to let yourself exist in the hollow space without forcing meaning. And if the minutes feel impossible, then just hold on to the next breath, and the one after that. You don't have to be okay; you just have to be here.",
