      "content": "That ache you're carrying is the heaviest thing in the world, and it's no wonder you're exhausted—grief like this can make even breathing feel like a chore. But that thought of \"being with him\" isn't peace; it's the pain lying to you, trying to convince you that the only way out is through the dark. You're not a burden for wanting relief, but you deserve a relief that lets you live, not one that ends you. The hollow ache will soften, not because he's forgotten, but because you'll learn to carry him differently. Right now, just let yourself be tired—you don't have to fight for hope today, just stay for the next hour.",
